%T A123470 407037501199
%N A123470 Number of 2-split Berge perfect graphs on n nodes.
%C A123470 A graph is 2-split if its vertex set can be partitioned into at most two cliques and at most two stable sets (a (2,2)-graph); the class is closed under induced subgraphs. The terms count the 2-split graphs that are also perfect, i.e. have no odd hole and no odd antihole (Strong Perfect Graph Theorem), up to isomorphism (Hougardy, 2006). - _Meghanto Majumder_, Oct 01 2026
%H A123470 S. Hougardy, <a href="http://www.or.uni-bonn.de/~hougardy/">Home Page</a>
%H A123470 S. Hougardy, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1016/j.disc.2006.05.021">Classes of perfect graphs</a>, Discr. Math. 306 (2006), 2529-2571.
%Y A123470 Cf. A000088, A052431 (perfect graphs).
